#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:1
msgid "How to publish a validated runtime authority"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:3
msgid ""
"Use this guide when you change Cadrumo's tax-rule registry or its legal "
"evidence. Publication turns validated Agencia Estatal de Administración "
"Tributaria (AEAT) modelo rules into the artifact the runtime reads for "
"calculations and filing exports. It is a development and release "
"operation, not an `aeat` command for taxpayers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:9
msgid ""
"The artifact is generated output. It records a digest of its own content "
"and the identity of the registry and evidence it was compiled from, so "
"the registry gate can tell when it is out of date. It is also the sole "
"shipped runtime source: installed code does not open the authored "
"registry tree or maintain a parallel cache of tables parsed from it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:15
msgid ""
"For the artifact format, runtime checks, error classes, and Python "
"application programming interface (API), see [Registry, legal sources, "
"and Python API](../reference/registry-legal-api.md). For an ordinary "
"installed-command failure, use [Diagnose and repair](troubleshooting.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:19
msgid "Publish"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:21
msgid "Start from a registry that passes the registry validation suite."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:22
msgid "From the repository root, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:28
msgid ""
"The command materializes authoring deltas into complete typed revisions, "
"validates the bundled registry and its source evidence, then atomically "
"replaces `src/cadrumo/_data/registry/authority/authority.json`. It prints"
" the artifact path and the identity digest it recorded. `--registry-"
"root`, `--source-root`, and `--artifact` select other trees or another "
"destination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:34
msgid ""
"Commit the regenerated `authority.json` together with the registry change"
" that required it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:37
msgid ""
"If validation is refused, or the registry changes while it is being "
"validated, publication fails and leaves the previous artifact byte-for-"
"byte in place. Don't edit the artifact by hand. Correct the registry, "
"then publish again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:41
msgid ""
"Publication also projects the shared `floor`, `horizon`, and optional "
"`hard_ceiling` support envelope and the typed runtime catalogues for IVA "
"rules, place of supply, countries and territories, recargo bands, and "
"apoderamiento scopes. Every required catalogue must be populated. Modelo "
"and tax-domain identifiers accept their stable syntax in code, but "
"membership belongs to this validated authority; an identifier absent from"
" its published vocabulary is not silently admitted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:49
msgid "Check that the artifact is current"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:51
msgid "Run the registry gate:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:57
msgid ""
"Its first step, `python -m dev.registry.conformance integrity`, exits 1 "
"with a refusal on standard error when the artifact is stale, unreadable, "
"or in an earlier format. The refusal names the recorded and the expected "
"identity digests and the command that republishes the artifact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:62
msgid ""
"The identity depends only on file content and on paths relative to the "
"registry and source roots. A fresh clone on any platform therefore agrees"
" with the publisher. A change to the compiler's code that doesn't touch "
"the registry or its evidence doesn't make the artifact stale. The full-"
"registry publication round-trip test covers the compiler itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:68
msgid "Recover from an invalid authority"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:70
msgid ""
"When an installed workflow refuses an unavailable, malformed, altered, or"
" unsupported-version artifact, stop the workflow. The "
"`bundled_authority()` load doesn't compile authoring sources, parse raw "
"TOML, repair an artifact, or fall back to a separately cached runtime "
"table."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:75
msgid ""
"Preserve the failed artifact when it is present, plus the package "
"version, artifact digest, error class, and redacted logs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:77
msgid ""
"Republish from a validated registry, and confirm that `just check-"
"registry` passes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:79
msgid "Rebuild the package so it contains the replacement artifact."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/publish-runtime-authority.md:81
msgid ""
"Escalate through the [project issue "
"tracker](https://github.com/nevenincs/cadrumo/issues) with the release "
"version, artifact digest, error class, and redacted log context. Never "
"include taxpayer data."
msgstr ""

